        "value": "critically endangered",
        "source": "elcat-v2024.1",
        "note": "ǂHoan is no longer passed on to the younger generations and is therefore no longer learnt as mother tongue (L1).  The mother tongue of the majority of [ǂHoan] children is the Bantu language Kgalagadi (S.31d), which is also the lingua franca of the region. [Endangerment.Certainty: 1]",
